From 30575e6d98e777f2a3df8ce5ea8190dffa803155 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 02:58:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00909/11171] [outer-loop] CPU-while-#1: close code caveat (A)
 + first ARC-domain verifier (C)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A — dedicated static code verifier caveat CLOSED: shipped ASTStructureVerifier added
to the formal-oracle code derisk; on the v2 semantic corpus it is ALSO ~chance
(single-feature AUROC ~0.5). Static code verification is execution-bound on semantics
BY DESIGN (targets structure/signature, which semantic failures preserve). Syntactic
class still cleanly caught (v1 learned 0.936).

C — first ARC-domain verifier (the north-star domain), on local ARC-AGI-1 public data
(400 tasks, gold solutions). Cheap rule-based structural-consistency PRUNER (dims/
palette/bg from train pairs; NO induction, NO LLM). Verdict: MODERATE structural pruner,
PRUNER_NOT_SELECTOR. Cleanly rejects STRUCTURALLY-malformed candidates (wrong-task 0.95,
random 0.89, wrong-dim 0.86); BLIND to CONTENT errors preserving structure (perturbed-
gold 0.006, transpose 0.29, blank 0.14). combined_top1 ~0.7% (cannot select gold
uniquely). This demonstrates the north-star division of labor on real ARC: verifier
PRUNES structural errors (efficiency axis), generator INDUCES content (accuracy axis).
Registry: arc_grid_structural_pruner (candidate). NEXT: object/symmetry invariants +
induced-rule grounding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
